/**
 * The complete fixed-service bundle returned by {@link SimCoreServiceAdapter#getCoreService} and
 * carried on {@link SimulationInput#coreService}: the network plus the core timetable.
 *
 * Grouping these four collections behind one value type is what lets the core-service source be
 * swapped (for a real GTFS feed, say) by reimplementing a single adapter method, without touching
 * {@link SimEngine} or the UI.
 *
 * Everything in here is **invariant across runs**. Baseline and every candidate allocation see
 * the same stops, routes, links and trips.
 */
type SimCoreServiceInput {

  /** Every {@link SimStop} in the scenario network. */
  stops: [SimStop]

  /** Every {@link SimRouteDef}, core and supplemental-eligible. */
  routes: [SimRouteDef]

  /** Every directed {@link SimTravelLink}, supplying baseline travel minutes. */
  travelLinks: [SimTravelLink]

  /** Every fixed {@link SimCoreTrip} scheduled within the simulation horizon. */
  coreTrips: [SimCoreTrip]
}
